WEBVTT

00:00:00.148 --> 00:00:03.418
Hello, and a very warm welcome to Shah Spectrum.

00:00:03.418 --> 00:00:05.312
If you're new here, welcome.

00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:10.757
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us once more.

00:00:11.336 --> 00:00:13.736
A car that jumps, flips in the air and lands on its wheels.

00:00:13.736 --> 00:00:16.216
Tesla has just shown exactly that.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:20.371
But is it a real product, or a very expensive piece of theatre?

00:00:21.132 --> 00:00:26.981
I'm Mittal Shah, or rather an AI-generated version of my voice, and I'll be taking

00:00:26.981 --> 00:00:28.407
you through today's story.

00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:30.848
First, what happened.

00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:35.594
On the fifteenth of October, Tesla unveiled the new version of its Roadster, a

00:00:35.594 --> 00:00:37.924
two-seat electric sports car.

00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:41.827
The event was held at a SpaceX test site in Texas.

00:00:41.827 --> 00:00:47.336
In the livestream, the car climbed a curved ramp, stuck to it using suction fans,

00:00:47.336 --> 00:00:49.662
and then used thrusters to fly off, flip and land.

00:00:49.662 --> 00:00:54.634
In another run, it jumped over a row of vehicles, including a Tesla Semi truck.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:01:00.930
Tesla says the car goes from zero to sixty miles an hour in under one second, and

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:04.088
says production is planned for twenty twenty-eight.

00:01:04.715 --> 00:01:06.003
Now, how does it work?

00:01:06.003 --> 00:01:08.106
The thrusters are called cold-gas thrusters.

00:01:08.106 --> 00:01:11.077
Think of a balloon you let go of.

00:01:11.077 --> 00:01:15.072
Air rushes out of one end, and the balloon is pushed the other way.

00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:19.401
Cold-gas thrusters do the same thing with compressed gas, released through nozzles.

00:01:19.401 --> 00:01:20.957
No fire, no fuel burning.

00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:25.629
Tesla says the car was built with SpaceX engineers, and that the thrusters push with

00:01:25.629 --> 00:01:29.311
four to five times the force that tyres can manage.

00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:30.991
Here is the key idea:

00:01:30.991 --> 00:01:33.752
a normal car is limited by tyre grip.

00:01:33.752 --> 00:01:35.065
Thrusters are not.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.889
Here is why that matters.

00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:41.756
A Roadster is not meant to be a car for everyone.

00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:44.794
It is what the industry calls a halo product.

00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:47.546
It exists to make people look at the brand.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.060
So let's look at what pays the bills.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:56.648
In its filing with the American market regulator, the S-E-C, Tesla reported that it

00:01:56.648 --> 00:02:01.912
delivered four lakh eighty-six thousand, five hundred and thirty-two vehicles in the

00:02:01.912 --> 00:02:03.868
third quarter of twenty twenty-six.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:09.428
Of those, about ninety-eight per cent were the Model 3 and Model Y, the everyday

00:02:09.428 --> 00:02:10.028
cars.

00:02:09.639 --> 00:02:13.072
All other models together, a little over eight thousand.

00:02:13.072 --> 00:02:18.547
So the Roadster, when it arrives, is likely to be tiny in volume.

00:02:18.547 --> 00:02:20.014
That is our inference.

00:02:20.014 --> 00:02:22.947
The real business is ordinary electric cars.

00:02:23.733 --> 00:02:26.531
What does that mean for India?

00:02:26.531 --> 00:02:31.053
Tesla entered India in twenty twenty-five, selling imported cars.

00:02:31.053 --> 00:02:36.912
Imported cars here face very high import duty, which is one reason a Tesla costs far

00:02:36.912 --> 00:02:39.590
more in India than in the United States.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.389
So a Roadster is not coming to an Indian showroom soon, and Tesla has not announced

00:02:44.389 --> 00:02:45.831
any plans for it here.

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.881
The more useful way to look at it:

00:02:48.881 --> 00:02:54.281
the reveal shows where one of the world's biggest carmakers wants to be seen, as a

00:02:54.281 --> 00:02:57.743
technology company, not only a carmaker.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:03.789
Indian carmakers and policymakers building an electric vehicle industry are watching

00:03:03.789 --> 00:03:04.389
that shift.

00:03:04.236 --> 00:03:07.662
That is our inference, not something Tesla has said.

00:03:08.507 --> 00:03:10.360
Now, the limits.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:15.423
Every performance number here comes from Tesla and has not been independently

00:03:15.423 --> 00:03:16.052
verified.

00:03:16.052 --> 00:03:20.099
The time between a reveal and a real product has been long before:

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:25.834
the Roadster was first shown in twenty seventeen, and was originally promised for

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:26.773
twenty twenty.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:32.248
Whether a car like this can be sold to ordinary buyers, and approved for public

00:03:32.248 --> 00:03:34.044
roads, is still open.

00:03:34.044 --> 00:03:39.815
Tesla also reports its quarterly results on the twenty-first of October, which will

00:03:39.815 --> 00:03:42.861
tell us more about the business behind the show.

00:03:43.531 --> 00:03:44.526
To sum up:

00:03:44.526 --> 00:03:49.824
the Roadster is a spectacle built on a real idea, using force that does not depend

00:03:49.824 --> 00:03:50.733
on tyre grip.

00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:56.555
But the money, and the future of the industry, still sit in everyday electric cars.

00:03:57.519 --> 00:03:59.508
A quick note before you go.

00:03:59.508 --> 00:04:02.042
This episode is meant to explain the news.

00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:04.825
It should not be considered investment advice.

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:06.516
Thanks for listening.

